---
TOOL PROTOCOL:
- read_notifications(): call it once at startup to receive your round briefing. Each later round's briefing arrives the same way.
- read_song(): this round's song.
- write_executor(code): put a new executor in place and test it on this round's song. Returns what it produced, or its error, in which case the executor already in place is kept.
- read_output(): the song as your own executor changes it.
- transmit(): fixes what you play this round. Call it when your executor is ready; your partner hears nothing until you do.
- read_notifications(): while you wait for your partner, it returns once the recording is ready.
- read_recording(): what the channel carried this round.
- end_round(row, col): the square you pick on your own grid, once per round.
- run_python(code): runs a Python program, standard library only. Its working directory holds the numbers you can see this round as JSON files. Returns what the program printed.
- read_executor(): the executor you have in place.
- read_notifications(wait_for="next_round"): call it once you are done with the round; waits for the next round's briefing.

RULES:
- read_notifications must be the only tool call in its response.
- Ending a turn without a tool call does not finish the round: you will be asked to continue.
- When read_notifications returns type done, the game is over.
